  it was the exact specific thing that we  were going to change  and it was global it was like i said it  was like 150 tasks overall dana had all  the pieces in front of her they just had  to be rearranged in a way that could  make the bigger picture easier to see  and much like the mystery of the game it  takes picking up pieces one at a time  and fitting them in with others until  you have the full scope of what's  happening  but it's like okay we're going to make  this quest line start here and that  affects these 18 other things and i had  like in detail list them all and it was  true like the list of tasks i wrote that  was it and it was done the time came to  submit the game for its street date when  there was no turning back whatever game  they shipped  that was it  there isn't going to be  a second chance no one is going to come  back with notes on this and say hey  here's how to improve it you've read so  many user research reports by now try to  think how they think and combine that  with your experience and instincts and  then filter that through what's possible  in two weeks and then just jump  ironically the process of redesigning  deathly was much like the puzzle players  and cult were facing in-game and the  final pieces only fell into place just  days before the game was officially  released  and when it was finally released well  in the beginning dana wanted to create  something that embraced her principles  of giving absolute freedom to the player  to reward them with their own sense of  discovery by giving them essentially  nothing in the end however she needed to  loosen her grip and strike a balance by  incorporating things like a guided tour  or ui tutorials and so on but even  despite the addition of those more  conventional tropes death loop managed  to retain a unique and unconventional  approach rarely seen in the aaa space so  yeah she may have added tutorials and  waypoints but our core principles  were unwavered you can play it safe and  still fail  wouldn't you rather feel spectacularly  doing something risky and dangerous and  crazy like given the option between  failing doing something safe and feeling  doing something dangerous i'll take the  other one because like failure isn't  inevitable but it comes like from things  totally out of your control it paid off  and not just in review scores but  for dana two  i am very proud of this game  might be the the game i'm the most proud  of that i've worked on  [Music]
 

